  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking, for EssyBus 3.0.0: ResetInterface is gone. The layer now repairs its own USB link: on a link fault reported by the driver (invalid handle, I/O error, device not found, ...) it stops the interrupt poller, reopens and configures the device, starts a new poller, and throws a PhysicalLayerException so EssyBus retries on the new link. A read timeout from a silent device no longer touches the link. Every handle access, the poller included, is under one lock, and a reset no longer leaves the old poller running. InterruptLineChange is renamed InterruptAsserted (as in EssyBus 3.0.0). New: LinkReopened event and IsLinkDown.",
